                <pb facs="0544" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859.01/146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-20T00:00:00-04:00">April 20,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3171. Your 3190, April 19, 5 p.m. The Department is agreeable to the suggestion
                    of the Foreign Office that an approach be made to the King before communicating
                    to the Soviet Government the proposed action regarding Denmark. It is assumed
                    that the Foreign Office will inform Clark Kerr regarding this change in
                    procedure, and that he, in turn, will notify Mr. Harriman.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
